CommitDate: Wed Oct 14 07:44:44 2026 -0500

    feat(df-1013-03): opt-in ?debug=search diagnostics on REST q= path
    
    Per-namespace searchFreshness/searchRebuilt/searchSkipReason existed only
    in the boot warm-up stderr summary; GET /api/memories?q= carried no signal
    about whether a first query paid an inline FTS rebuild or used a warm
    index, and DUCKBRAIN_SEARCH_TIMING=1 logs to stderr only.
    
    - ?debug=search (only accepted value; requires q=) appends a `searchDebug`
      object to the response: indexFreshness/indexRebuilt/indexSkipReason,
      keywordCandidates/semanticCandidates, cacheHits/uniqueMisses,
      embedMs/queryEmbedMs. Without the flag the response shape is unchanged.
    - Timing data is collected through onTiming collectors on semanticSearch
      (src/embedding/search.ts) and keywordSearch (src/search/query.ts) — the
      same ensureFreshness state the warm-up summary reports, so the two
      surfaces cannot disagree.
    - AC-2 test proves warmNamespace().searchFreshness ("missing"→rebuild)
      agrees with the request-time searchDebug.indexFreshness ("fresh") for
      the same namespace.
    - Docs: docs/api/http-api.md documents the flag, field semantics, and an
      example response; the allow-list/docs drift test stays green.
    
    Addresses DF-1013-03.
    
    Co-authored-by: Alexis Okuwa <wojonstech@gmail.com>
